{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nIndependent validation confirmed stale rollout headers at `mapping_config.py:1-22`, adapter headers, and `apply_outbound.py:80-88`; arbitration prose conflicts with `outbound_differ.py:234`; `OutboundDiffConfig` documents five values despite nine at `outbound_differ.py:217-262,511-524`; and `docs/env-vars.md:149,153` omits rollback semantics.\n\n## Approach\n\nCorrect the maintained source headers and authoritative operator material to reflect current behavior. Treat `docs/env-vars.md` as generated: update its source metadata or provide an authoritative operator page plus generated link, never hand-edit generated output. Document the verified five-field baseline arbitration and consumer-specific legacy create-route effects.\n\n## Scope\n\n- reconciler module headers and outbound configuration documentation\n- authoritative rollback/config documentation and generated env-var output/source\n- documentation tests or generation checks\n\n## Testing\n\nRegenerate affected documentation, run its drift check, and verify the stated examples against focused arbitration/create-route tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Rollout headers describe active mappings, Cloud/DC transport, and create/update paths.\n- [x] Documentation states that the five inbound-mirrored fields suppress outbound write only when local equals stored baseline; local changes, conflicts, non-arbitrated fields, and incomplete baselines retain local behavior.\n- [x] All nine `OutboundDiffConfig` fields and explicit `mapping=`/`repo_root=` precedence over config values are documented.\n- [x] Rollback documentation gives accepted values, defaults, and consumer-specific effects without claiming `legacy` always deletes.\n- [x] [non-codebase] Generated env-var documentation is regenerated from an authoritative source and its drift check passes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788419135369454001,"uuid":"7d4123d5-3d39-4819-a817-57fec9f0d357"}